abstract:
The workhorse of tabular machine learning. Start with the mean, fit a tree to the residuals, add a shrunken version of it, repeat. We derive why the residual is exactly the negative gradient of squared loss, reproduce the notes' worked residual table by hand, extend the identical machinery to classification through log-odds, and measure what the learning rate and the number of trees actually do.}
